          "text": {
            "text": "The train station itself is pretty typical for London\u2014busy, loud, and always full of people rushing somewhere\u2014but it works surprisingly well. The signs are easy enough to follow, so even if you\u2019re not familiar with the area, you can find your platform without feeling totally overwhelmed. There are a few small spots to grab food or a drink, which is nice when you\u2019re waiting around. The atmosphere can be a little hectic at peak times, but that\u2019s kind of expected, and the staff usually manage to keep things moving.\n\nOverall, it\u2019s not the kind of place you\u2019d go out of your way to visit, but it does what it needs to do. Trains come fairly regularly, delays happen but not constantly, and getting in and out is generally straightforward. It\u2019s one of those places that doesn\u2019t try to impress you\u2014it just gets you where you need to go, and honestly, that\u2019s enough.",
            "languageCode": "en"
          },
