          "text": {
            "text": "I go through here once a week with my kids and I always see grown adults push through the barriers and never stopped. They often push behind me and my children. Not one staff member bats an eye lid. However, this evening I tried to go through with my son and I was aggressively stopped by a staff member asking for my son\u2019s age. I told him to look carefully as my son actually has a pass on him and we are paying customers. His age is not their business. He told me he \u201cthought\u201d we were going to go through together. And really, so what if we did at this point? He is a child at the end of the day (still in primary school might I add) and at this very station you always have adults jumping barriers but staff obviously make a beeline and try to intimidate children as they are easier targets. Granted the fare dodging is an issue in many stations. Maybe focus on the real culprits rather than primary school age children.",
            "languageCode": "en"
          },
